From: overpressure <overpressure@pico4>
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: build on its own again

Valve's squashed iris series moves Venus under vcodec/ and switches it to the queue and firmware
code it shares with iris, but leaves hfi_venus.c and core.c on the old names: Venus no longer
compiles, and only iris is built for the Frame. This gives Venus back its own files as they were
before the series (its firmware loader and queues), in their new place; iris keeps the shared
code. SM8250's codec is Venus (the series' iris knows only SM8550).
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/Makefile b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/Makefile
index 6abd54a97f4b..91ee6be10292 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/vcodec/venus/Makefile
@@ -1,15 +1,12 @@
